(4240779, 605079, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this is a strong balanced photograph.  The statue being on the right third works well.<br/> <br/>Technically, the focus is good and shows the texture of the statue very well, as well as the wall.  The bw conversion you have used is nice, and I like the dramatic shadows.  I kinda like the brick wall in the background, but it gives more a "modern" feeling to the shot, somehow, and detracts from the "oldness" of the statue, I think.  A profile with the tree might have been the better angle.  Also, if you could have had a more shallow dof to slightly blur the bricks, it might have made a bit of a difference.<br/> <br/>Overall, this is a technically well done photo.  There are no obvious flaws in the execution.  It meets the challenge.  I suspect,though, that it didn''t "connect" with the viewers on any level other an an emotional one.<br/> <br/>If I need to further clarify or explain myself, please feel free to contact me.  Thanks for your participation!<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, this is a strong balanced photograph.  The statue being on the right third works well. Technically, the focus is good and shows the texture of the statue very well, as well as the wall.  The bw conversion you have used is nice, and I like the dramatic shadows.  I kinda like the brick wall in the background, but it gives more a "modern" feeling to the shot, somehow, and detracts from the "oldness" of the statue, I think.  A profile with the tree might have been the better angle.  Also, if you could have had a more shallow dof to slightly blur the bricks, it might have made a bit of a difference. Overall, this is a technically well done photo.  There are no obvious flaws in the execution.  It meets the challenge.  I suspect,though, that it didn''t "connect" with the viewers on any level other an an emotional one. If I need to further clarify or explain myself, please feel free to contact me.  Thanks for your participation! karmat', '2007-11-12 10:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4240808, 606501, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Welcome to dpc!<br/> <br/>Compositionally, your shot feels a bit static.  I think this is probably due to the fact that it is the center, vertically, of the picture.  Moving it up in the frame, or down (probably the better choice) would give it a more dynamic, balanced feeling.  <br/> <br/>Technically, the focus and exposure is good.  The saturation is a bit high making the greens look almost unnatural.  Maybe bringing the greens down just a bit would help.<br/> <br/>Overall, it is an interesting shot.  A boat tied to a tree when no water is around -- that is kinda funny.  However, it looks like you were just walking around and saw it and snapped it.  Different angles of perspective could really make this an interesting photograph.  Getting down on the ground, shooting from the stern, and filling the frame with just the front of the boat are just some of the possibilities.  Also, the peeling paint could make for some nice texture shots.<br/> <br/>You picked a good subject, and it is technically okay, but there is a lot more that could be done to make it even more interesting.<br/> <br/>Best wishes to you in future challenges and if I can further clarify or explain myself, please feel free to contact me.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Welcome to dpc! Compositionally, your shot feels a bit static.  I think this is probably due to the fact that it is the center, vertically, of the picture.  Moving it up in the frame, or down (probably the better choice) would give it a more dynamic, balanced feeling.   Technically, the focus and exposure is good.  The saturation is a bit high making the greens look almost unnatural.  Maybe bringing the greens down just a bit would help. Overall, it is an interesting shot.  A boat tied to a tree when no water is around -- that is kinda funny.  However, it looks like you were just walking around and saw it and snapped it.  Different angles of perspective could really make this an interesting photograph.  Getting down on the ground, shooting from the stern, and filling the frame with just the front of the boat are just some of the possibilities.  Also, the peeling paint could make for some nice texture shots. You picked a good subject, and it is technically okay, but there is a lot more that could be done to make it even more interesting. Best wishes to you in future challenges and if I can further clarify or explain myself, please feel free to contact me. karmat', '2007-11-12 10:59:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4240914, 605828, 29011, '<td valign="top">Congratulations with the nice finish :)<br/>Nicely composed and the tone of choice does give it an old world look. <br/> <br/>Funny comments you got there LOL. No "my bad on the title" , it is an Adobe. I got it without using much brain power. I do watch National Geographic ;) But I won''t lie and say abode didn''t cross my mind. An adobe abode, hehe.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-12 11:37:39.</i></td>', 'Congratulations with the nice finish :)Nicely composed and the tone of choice does give it an old world look.  Funny comments you got there LOL. No "my bad on the title" , it is an Adobe. I got it without using much brain power. I do watch National Geographic ;) But I won''t lie and say abode didn''t cross my mind. An adobe abode, hehe.', '2007-11-12 11:36:33.000000', '2007-11-12 11:37:39.000000', 0),
(4240985, 606484, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Brin,<br/>       Very nice image, peaceful &amp; calming. I really like your composition all the elements come together extremely well. I also like the way you framed it all in, the placement of the tree &amp; brush line in the foreground are well done &amp; the cottage is very well placed. I also like the use of the slope here gives us a three dimensional feel for the image. I like the tonality here it all works really well. If there is one thing that hit me &amp; I am not sure there is much you could have done about it is the tree trunk, it was the very first thing that caught my eye. The blackness of the trunk in relation to the rest of the tree &amp; overall image is a bit of a distraction it just kept drawing my eye. Overall this is a wonderful image like I said very peaceful &amp; calm.</td>', 'Hi Brin,       Very nice image, peaceful & calming. I really like your composition all the elements come together extremely well. I also like the way you framed it all in, the placement of the tree & brush line in the foreground are well done & the cottage is very well placed. I also like the use of the slope here gives us a three dimensional feel for the image. I like the tonality here it all works really well. If there is one thing that hit me & I am not sure there is much you could have done about it is the tree trunk, it was the very first thing that caught my eye. The blackness of the trunk in relation to the rest of the tree & overall image is a bit of a distraction it just kept drawing my eye. Overall this is a wonderful image like I said very peaceful & calm.', '2007-11-12 11:53:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4241075, 606086, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Kae,<br/> <br/>      Wonderful image ! I love the lighting here think it makes the image. The composition is very well done, &amp; the framing is excellent. The tonality is also well done. What can I say, I love the image I think it was under rated by many I would have given this an 8 had I scored it. Nice work !!!!</td>', 'Hi Kae,       Wonderful image ! I love the lighting here think it makes the image. The composition is very well done, & the framing is excellent. The tonality is also well done. What can I say, I love the image I think it was under rated by many I would have given this an 8 had I scored it. Nice work !!!!', '2007-11-12 12:22:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4241244, 606397, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>This image definitely fits the challenge, as any tree that requires a "cane" to hold its limb up must be old.  However, there are two major issues that hurt your score on this.  First, the tree blends into the background way too much.  It is possible that shooting at a different time of day (different lighting) could have helped provide more separation between the tree and the background.  Second, I understand that you only had one shot left on your battery but this image is of a tree from a straight on perspective.  Without a unique perspective, it shouts snapshot to the voters.  Since nothing about this shot conveys Robin Hood besides your title, you need to find someway for this tree to tell a story on its own.  It is entirely possible that there may not be a story to tell.<br/> <br/>Feel free to send me a PM if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, This image definitely fits the challenge, as any tree that requires a "cane" to hold its limb up must be old.  However, there are two major issues that hurt your score on this.  First, the tree blends into the background way too much.  It is possible that shooting at a different time of day (different lighting) could have helped provide more separation between the tree and the background.  Second, I understand that you only had one shot left on your battery but this image is of a tree from a straight on perspective.  Without a unique perspective, it shouts snapshot to the voters.  Since nothing about this shot conveys Robin Hood besides your title, you need to find someway for this tree to tell a story on its own.  It is entirely possible that there may not be a story to tell. Feel free to send me a PM if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-11-12 13:24:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4241274, 606778, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>A straight on shot of a rotten pumpkin, what''s not to love about that?  For your chosen subject matter, I think you got about as much out of this image as there was to get.  The focus and post processing are pretty good and the colors look realistic on my computer.  This image falls into the not DPC friendly category, as the subject matter is not very appealing.<br/> <br/>You need to do more than just meet the challenge at DPC to get a good score.  The winners show creativity, have an interesting perspective, and tell a story.  Keep entering challenges and you will find that you will improve with practice.<br/> <br/>Feel free to send me a PM if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, A straight on shot of a rotten pumpkin, what''s not to love about that?  For your chosen subject matter, I think you got about as much out of this image as there was to get.  The focus and post processing are pretty good and the colors look realistic on my computer.  This image falls into the not DPC friendly category, as the subject matter is not very appealing. You need to do more than just meet the challenge at DPC to get a good score.  The winners show creativity, have an interesting perspective, and tell a story.  Keep entering challenges and you will find that you will improve with practice. Feel free to send me a PM if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-11-12 13:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
